---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE_NAME, OPERATOR_NAME, PRICE, EMAIL, GUARANTEE_FULL, RE_INSPECTION_FEE } from "../config";

const lastUpdated = "23 July 2026";
---
<Layout
  title="Terms of Service | Pool Compliance Melbourne"
  description="Terms of service for Pool Compliance Melbourne, a booking service operated by CertCycle for independent pool and spa barrier inspections."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: "Terms of Service", path: "/terms/" }]} />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-navy-900 mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-500 mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose-content">
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of this website and our booking service. By booking through
        {SITE_NAME}, operated by {OPERATOR_NAME}, you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Our role as a booking service</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} is a booking service. We are not a pool safety inspection company, and we do not carry out
        pool or spa barrier inspections ourselves. All inspections are performed by independent, third-party
        inspectors registered with the Building and Plumbing Commission (BPC) specifically for pool barrier
        compliance. When you book through us, we arrange and coordinate an inspection with one of these independent
        inspectors on your behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Bookings and pricing</h2>
      <p>
        Our standard fee for a residential pool or spa barrier inspection is {PRICE}, inclusive of the inspection
        and the Form 23 Certificate of Barrier Compliance if your barrier passes. {GUARANTEE_FULL} This free
        re-inspection applies only where the original inspection was booked through us. Re-inspections following an
        inspection originally carried out by a different provider, and any re-inspection beyond the first, are
        charged at {RE_INSPECTION_FEE} (or our standard {PRICE} fee where a different provider carried out the
        original inspection).
      </p>
      <p>
        Prices are current at the time of publishing and may be updated from time to time. The price confirmed at
        the time of your booking will apply to that booking.
      </p>

      <h2>Scheduling</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to schedule inspections within 48 hours of booking, subject to inspector availability and reasonable
        access to your property. Scheduling times are estimates, not guaranteed windows, and may be affected by
        factors outside our control, including weather and inspector availability.
      </p>

      <h2>Cancellations and rescheduling</h2>
      <p>
        You can cancel or reschedule a booking by contacting us with reasonable notice. Repeated late cancellations
        or missed appointments without notice may affect our ability to offer future scheduling flexibility.
      </p>

      <h2>Inspection outcomes</h2>
      <p>
        Whether a barrier passes or fails inspection is determined solely by the independent, BPC-registered
        inspector who attends your property, based on their professional assessment against the applicable
        Victorian pool and spa barrier standard. We do not influence, guarantee, or have visibility into an
        inspection outcome in advance of the inspector's assessment.
      </p>

      <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Providing accurate contact and property details when booking.</li>
        <li>Providing reasonable access to the pool or spa barrier area at the scheduled time.</li>
        <li>Arranging and paying for any repairs identified as necessary to pass an inspection.</li>
        <li>Lodging your Form 23 Certificate of Barrier Compliance with your local council within the required 30-day window.</li>
        <li>Ensuring your pool or spa is registered with your local council, where required.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, {OPERATOR_NAME} is not liable for any loss or damage arising from
        the acts or omissions of independent inspectors, delays in scheduling, or your failure to meet council
        registration or lodgement obligations. Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any consumer
        guarantee, right or remedy under the Australian Consumer Law that cannot lawfully be excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>Website use</h2>
      <p>
        The content on this website is provided for general information about Victorian pool and spa barrier
        compliance and is not a substitute for professional advice about your specific property. While we aim to
        keep information accurate and current, requirements can change, and you should confirm details relevant to
        your situation with your inspector or local council where it matters.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of Victoria, Australia, and any disputes arising from them are subject
        to the jurisdiction of Victorian courts.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The updated version will be posted on this page with a revised
        "last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms can be directed to {EMAIL}.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
